    "title": "Phrase of the week",
    "text": "Selling like hotcakes: Originating in the United States in the 1840s, it came from the fact pancakes traditionally were cooked and served in large batches at outdoor fairs, markets or after church. Because they were cheap, fresh and piping hot, hungry crowds bought them up faster than the cooks could flip them, creating an image of rapid, high-volume sales.",
